.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
.Dd October 27, 2026
.Dt MOOBFS-INDEX 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm moobfs-index
.Nd answer MoobFS attribute queries in user space
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl -uid Ar N
.Op Fl -domain
.Op Fl -json
.Op Fl -order Ar name type Cm asc | desc
.Op Fl -limit Ar N
.Ar directory
.Op Ar term ...
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
walks
.Ar directory ,
reads every typed attribute with the encoding the kernel uses and answers the same conjunctive
queries as the MoobFS layer's QUERY and QUERY2, printing
.Dq ino<TAB>path
lines.
It is the oracle the test suite compares the kernel with.
MoobFS is an experimental research project.
.Pp
With
.Fl -json ,
print one JSON object with the directory argument
.Dq dir ,
the number of emitted entries
.Dq count ,
and an ordered
.Dq results
array.
Each result has an integer
.Dq ino
and a path relative to the directory
.Dq path .
The JSON shape is experimental and may change; see docs/tools.md.
.Pp
A
.Ar term
is four words,
.Dq name op type value ,
up to four terms joined by AND; op is one of
.Cm eq , lt , le , gt , ge , prefix
or
.Cm exists ,
whose type and value are given as
.Dq - .
An operator ending in
.Sq \&?
(for example
.Cm gt? )
also matches files without the attribute.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl -uid Ar N
switch to uid and gid
.Ar N
first; run as root, also drop every supplementary group, so the walk sees only what that uid
and gid reach
.It Fl -domain
treat
.Ar directory
as a domain directory: its own attributes are left out and an entry is listed only when it
passes the homogeneity rule, evaluated independently of the kernel
.It Fl -json
print the results as one JSON document
.It Fl -order Ar name type Cm asc | desc
list only entries whose
.Ar name
attribute has
.Ar type ,
sorted by value and inode number; terms may then be empty
.It Fl -limit Ar N
keep the first
.Ar N
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
0 on success, non-zero on a usage error or a failed walk.
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Dl $ moobfs-index --domain /srv/memories/alice kind eq string decision
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr moobfs-attr 1 ,
.Xr moobfs-check 1
.Pp
docs/spec-query-v2.md in the MoobFS repository,
.Lk https://github.com/studiomoob/llmoobfs
